reference = "Also called melamine resin or melamine formaldehyde. It is a hard thermosetting plastic often used for kitchen utensils and plates (Melmac), and is the main constituent of Formica and laminate flooring (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melamine_resin). Density and formula from Table 51.2 of Hungerford (1960)."

