reference = "Weight fractions are calculated based on the 13 compounds in shale in Table 7.1 of Blatt et al. (2006). Average density of shale = 2.76 g/cm3 in Table 6.1.5 of Avallone and Baumeister III (1996). Density = 2.68 g/cm3 for solid shale and 1.59 g/cm3 for broken shale at http://www.simetric.co.uk/si_materials.htm (Walker 2009). Density = 2.4 to 2.8 g/cm3, and bulk density = 1.47 g/cm3, in Table 51.65 of Hungerford (1960). Bulk density = 1.47 in Table 6.1.5 of Avallone and Baumeister III (1996)."

